# Build-time inputs, never read at run time: patch-package applies patches/
# to node_modules during npm ci, before esbuild compiles the patched code
# into the bundles.
patches/**

# Local tooling
#
# vsce reads only this file and its own defaults, never .gitignore, so
# whatever a local checkout holds that git ignores (a code-graph index, an
# assistant's session memory, an MCP config that can carry tokens) ships in a
# locally packaged VSIX unless a line here drops it. CI packages a fresh
# checkout, so a release build never shows the gap.
#
# No top-level dot-file or dot-folder is part of the extension, so these two
# lines drop them all, including a tool nobody has listed yet: `.*` the files,
# `.*/**` everything under the folders (vsce appends `/**` only to a line
# with no wildcard in its last segment). Both match the top level only.
.*
.*/**
# Three of them at any depth too (.git, .vscode, .idea), as a dependency can
# carry them.
**/.git/**
**/.vscode/**
**/.idea/**
# A non-dot tool has to be named: the extension's own top-level content is
# non-dot too, and keeping it while dropping unknown names would take `!`
# lines (see "How vsce reads this file" below).
graft/**
opencode.json
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
specs/**

# Media file
media/demo-jump-host.gif

# Node modules
#
# The extension is bundled by esbuild (esbuild.mjs, scripts/buildConfigs.mjs).
# The only thing a bundle loads from node_modules at run time is serialport
# (the serial sidecar's `external`) plus its own dependency closure. Every
# other production dependency is compiled into dist/*.js, or left out on
# purpose because ssh2 runs without it (cpu-features, ssh2's optional native
# accelerator, and the native-build helpers nan and buildcheck). Shipping
# their files is dead weight: nothing loads them, yet VSIX scanners report
# them. (npm audit --omit=dev still covers them through package-lock.json.)
#
# How vsce reads this file: a file is dropped when ANY ignore line matches it
# and NO `!` line does. Line order plays no part and a `!` line beats every
# ignore line, so never add a `!node_modules/...` line: a former
# `!node_modules/**/*.d.ts` kept the type definitions of excluded packages
# (tweetnacl/nacl.d.ts among them) in the VSIX.
#
# Adding a production dependency? If esbuild bundles it, add
# `node_modules/<name>/**` below. If a bundle loads it from disk (an
# `external` in scripts/buildConfigs.mjs) it must NOT be listed.
# test/unit/vsixPackaging.test.ts derives both facts from package-lock.json
# and fails either way.
node_modules/.package-lock.json
node_modules/ssh2/**
node_modules/asn1/**
node_modules/bcrypt-pbkdf/**
node_modules/tweetnacl/**
node_modules/safer-buffer/**
node_modules/cpu-features/**
node_modules/nan/**
node_modules/buildcheck/**
node_modules/esbuild/**
node_modules/@rollup/**
node_modules/rollup/**
node_modules/@nodable/entities/**
node_modules/anynum/**
node_modules/dhcp/**
node_modules/fast-xml-builder/**
node_modules/fast-xml-parser/**
node_modules/ip-address/**
node_modules/is-unsafe/**
node_modules/jsonc-parser/**
node_modules/minimist/**
node_modules/path-expression-matcher/**
node_modules/smart-buffer/**
node_modules/socks/**
node_modules/strnum/**
node_modules/xml-naming/**

